# bashtion-wasm — response headers for the statically-served files.
# split.sh copies this to public/_headers. Applies to every static asset,
# including the page and the pthread worker script (so the worker context
# inherits the same CSP). The three large files are served by worker.js, which
# sets its own headers.
#
# Two of these headers are FUNCTIONAL, not just hardening:
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy + Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy switch on
#   cross-origin isolation, without which SharedArrayBuffer (and therefore the
#   whole multi-threaded engine) will not start.
# And one CSP token is load-bearing:
#   'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets the engine JIT translation blocks into fresh
#   WebAssembly modules at runtime. It permits wasm compilation ONLY — not
#   JavaScript eval(). Remove it and the VM cannot run.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains

# Fingerprinted / immutable bundles: cache hard. (The HTML is intentionally
# left on the default short cache so page updates propagate.) The lab disk is
# deliberately NOT here: it belongs to the snapshot set, is renamed with it
# (load-lab.v3.data), and at ~200 KB can afford to revalidate - an immutable
# rule on a fixed name is what would strand a browser on an old disk.
# Nothing that comes from the engine build is here either (#74). out.js names
# the engine it was built with (qemu-system-x86_64.<hash>.wasm, see
# pack-site.sh), so it has to revalidate for a new engine to reach anyone; the
# engine itself is immutable in worker.js, under a name that cannot be reused.
# vendor/ (xterm-pty must be the version the engine linked) and load-rom.data
# (the fork tree's ROMs, which vm.state carries its own copy of and checks the
# size of) are that build's too, under fixed names, and are small.
/load-kernel.data
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
